  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;Due to the overall amount of built form, scale and massing across a constraint plot of land, the proposed development unacceptable as it would create a poorly-designed, cramped and incongruous scheme that would constitute an over-development of the site, to the detriment of the existing character and appearance of the host site and wider surrounding area accordance with policies D1 and D4 of the London Plan (2021), Policy 53 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By virtue of it excessive height, massing and siting, in close proximity to the site boundaries, as well as introduction of windows and terracing to the north west elevation, the proposed new building would unduly impact on neighbouring amenity at Nos. 10 to 14 Carlton Road in terms of the build form appearing overbearing, creating a loss of outlook, overlooking and a loss of privacy to existing occupants. As such, the proposal would fail to comply with Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by virtue of its excessive massing and close proximity between the subject buildings, would result in direct overlooking between proposed residential units with habitable rooms directly fronting rear elevation and balconies. The close proximity of the structures would create a loss of outlook, overlooking and a loss of privacy to proposed occupants, therefore adversely impacting residential amenity in conflict with Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The 3-bed 5-person unit over two storeys would fall short of the required Technical Space Standards in terms of gross internal area at the detriment to the quality of accommodation for proposed occupants. Therefore, the proposed development fails to comply with the requirements of Policies D4 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 56 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Due to insufficient information in respect to the Outline Construction Logistics Plan, the application fails to adequately demonstrate how the proposed development could be built or serviced without impacting or affecting the surrounding public highway and its network during construction. The proposal would be contrary to Policy T7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 65 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18.6667px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;he applicant has failed to enter into a S106 agreement and therefore not in compliance with Policy 94 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and the Waltham Forest Supplementary Planning Document “Planning Obligations” SPD, specifically in relation to the following planning obligations requirements (figures applicable at the time of the assessment of the application).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A) Highways:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;i) Car Free Development - the development is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be eligible for parking permits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ii) £5000 contribution to sustainable transport modes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;III) £750 towards CLP monitoring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;B) SAMMS&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;i) A financial contribution of £627 (per new unit) towards Strategic Access Management and Monitoring measures (SAMMs).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;D) Legal Fees:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;i) Payment of the Council’s legal fees for the preparation and completion of the Legal Agreement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ii) Monitoring Fee - A financial contribution towards the implementation and monitoring of and securing compliance with the S106, equal to 5% of the total of all other financial contributions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18.6667px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
